t(22, 545, """I say to our youth, believing in Allah Almighty's promise to our Ummah .. Prepare for the return, by the power of Allah your Great Lord .. hallowed be His names .. For no infrastructure .. no houses .. and no real wealth that suffices a person and exceeds his need will you find except in the Middle East, Allah willing""")

t(22, 1885, """Reducing the amount of technological "eye-dazzle" reduces the self's belief in everlasting life on earth without end .. Ultra-modern production by technology, which makes man feel as if he has reached the height of control and dominance on earth, this kind of hyper-modern production is a great and mighty enemy of the spirit, because it is a very high pleasure for the self, so it makes the self surpass the spirit and overcome it""")

t(23, 795, """The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ("The worst food is the food of the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out; and whoever does not come to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.")
Narrator: Abu Hurayrah | Scholar: al-Bukhari | Source: Sahih al-Bukhari
Page or number: 5177 | Summary of the scholar's ruling: [Authentic]
Sourcing: Reported by al-Bukhari (5177) and Muslim (1432)""")

t(24, 1000, """The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams; he slaughtered them with his own hand, said the name of Allah and the takbir, and placed his foot on their sides.
Summary of the scholar's ruling: [Authentic]
Narrator: Anas ibn Malik | Scholar: al-Bukhari | Source: Sahih al-Bukhari | Page or number: 5565 | Sourcing: Reported by al-Bukhari and Muslim""")

t(24, 2470, """Two elements bridge what has happened to us as an Ummah .. wealth and freedom""")

t(25, 2480, """The world order""")

t(26, 1270, """Morning exercise .. Days to come, by Allah Almighty's leave, in these streets""")

t(26, 2500, """And mornings on that day will not be like our mornings today .. So be of good cheer, and do not let the fools drag you into feebleness, weakness and despair while you are drawing near, by the power of your Great Lord, to what He promised your Prophet concerning you""")

t(27, 1345, """The concept of sending and transferring money will change .. Free sending .. No Western Union and its sisters .. Many concepts will change because of humanity's return to metal currency (gold) in that era""")

t(28, 165, """In the novel "The End" - the final chapter: Why did you kill your sister who was raped in the regime's prisons? Do you know that your punishment is now execution?""")

t(29, 250, """Liberating husbands who are wronged in their homes by women who do not fear Allah is an act of nearness to Allah Almighty, just like the nearness of liberating wronged women""")

t(29, 1560, """A noble prophetic hadith with a sound chain .. It contains a phrase .. Woe to every unjust wife who persists in wronging and hurting her husband, from that phrase in the noble hadith! I do not know the unseen that I should invent it, O our brothers the men, but it is glad tidings for those of you who live with unjust wives .. For in a society whose men are given wealth by the handful, while there are wives ungrateful to their spouses who do not fear Allah regarding their husbands, and the husbands who are given wealth by the handful want to divorce their wives, how easy divorce is in that time; that is a time unlike this time .. That is a stage in which the wronged husband will not be unable to rescue himself from an unjust wife who persists in injustice, or from a wife who has spent a lifetime hurting her husband while he stayed silent and patient, so he came to hate her and no longer feels it possible to love her again, yet in the time of capitalism he cannot get rid of her. This is the handing out and overflowing of wealth: men and women take from it what they need, and on that day the face of social life will change greatly.""")

t(29, 2230, """A door that will be opened, by Allah Almighty's leave, to liberate the women of the Ummah of Islam from injustice, oppression and aggression in marital homes where injustice and oppression run rampant""")

t(30, 1065, """A noble prophetic hadith with a sound chain .. It contains a phrase .. Woe to every unjust husband who persists in wronging his wife, from that phrase! I do not know the unseen that I should invent it, O our brothers the men .. But in a society whose men are given wealth by the handful, when one of its married women comes to dislike her husband and wants khul', the state ransoms her with state money and returns the dowry to the unjust husband who persists in injustice, and she marries anew a husband other than him; that is a time unlike this time .. That is a stage in which the wronged woman will not be unable to ransom herself from an unjust husband who persists in injustice, or from a husband who has spent a lifetime hurting her, so she came to hate him and no longer feels it possible to love him again. This is the handing out and overflowing of wealth: men and women take from it what they need, and on that day the face of social life will change greatly.""")

t(30, 1575, """And tranquility returns to the spouses and life is set right .. so there are no doors flung open to injustice from either side""")

t(31, 395, """So the rak'ahs increase, the charities grow great, and of the verses is recited what verses follow; the Lord is glorified with the utmost glorification, and He is exalted, praised and asked for forgiveness at every time and moment. Hearts are joined, tears dry, faces smile, good spreads in the world, and people's transgression against one another and evil perish in it. The houses of the Most Merciful fill with men and women who remember Him, and of our Ummah it is said in the Highest Assembly: blessed are they, for they obeyed the Lord and glorified Him, and became Muhammadan in their morals, like his companions who obeyed the Prophet Muhammad and revered him. On earth they did not transgress against any weak one, and they were a mercy and a good to the nations. They did what Allah wanted them to do and established the pure Muhammadan life, so they became an example for humanity. From the other nations came to them refugees, workers and specialists; they worked, earned and drew near to the followers of this religion, saw the goodness of its followers and submitted to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and became their brothers in the faith. They settled in a land wet with the tears of humble men and women, abandoned homelands that no longer benefited them, loved the abode of faith and saw in it their dwelling and resting place. The people of the land and its inhabitants rejoiced in them, the stranger became with them one of its inhabitants, and all became equal in giving. They were joined together, for they are the noble companions. They remained in this state for years that were blessed; their time was not scant in blessing like that which passed over the people before them, and they were granted many years of contentment. And if it is said "seven", then, Allah willing, they are not like people's seven today, which are like a speck. While they are in that state, Allah permits the world a farewell; events occur about which there is no doubt or dispute; the world quickens its steps toward its end, and events race to cast away all that remains in its hands. For a year, a month and a week a gloom bearable for the soul overshadows the people, and a hardship befalls them that is neither prolonged nor slight. The test ends and the Messiah comes; the transgressor is killed and no longer roams Allah's earth. People on that day have become few; most companions and loved ones have departed to their Lord and gone, leaving behind them a few of the few. The Messiah is a solace to them as if he were a paradise; they rejoice in Allah's recompense to them, are content with a life unlike the one they were used to, and know they will not be returned to the world's past. The years pass over them, and the last of them await the promised wind that will be gentle to them and will take their souls while they are joyful and at peace. After it no House is visited in pilgrimage and no prophet is visited, no verses are recited and no rak'ahs are prayed; the Qur'an is lifted and Ramadan does not return. The rest live the life of ignorance and are the worst of people on earth, a remnant of a remnant. Then Allah Almighty commands all wombs and they become barren; no child is born, and the matter is in women's throats like bitter colocynth. Son and mother copulate after they have despaired of mercy and realised that they kicked away every call to good a thousand times over. Then Allah Almighty decrees in His earth and His heaven what is no concern of ours.""")

t(31, 1610, """From the nation of treasures and gold to the nations of toil and fatigue .. When the news of this end of time comes to you, know that the term of the last seven has drawn near for us and for you, or the last eight for us and for you .. or the last nine for us and for you .. Then there is no seven, no eight and no nine after them .. only one human caravan preparing for the collective departure to Allah the Great .. So work, toil and tire yourselves .. For the nation of treasures and gold will be asked about itself, and you will be asked about yourselves .. As for the nation of treasures and gold, it will be asked: Were treasures not opened to you as they were never opened to those before you? They will all say: Yes, and bear witness against themselves. As for the one who falls short toward Allah the Great, our Lord, hallowed be His names and attributes, and falls short in the right of His servants by wronging them and devouring rights, he has no argument on that day after his wealth, his riches and his ease of living, which did not exist in his own nation or in the nations before it. And as for the one who worships Allah Almighty as He should be worshipped in the 7, the eight or the 9, and fears Allah his Lord regarding those below him, he has passed the test of the treasures of the 9, the eight or the 7 and was not led astray. You are heading toward the test of the treasures and you do not know, except those among us on whom Allah had mercy and whom He taught; such a one has known and learned. As for the people on the pulpits, they are heedless of that, and neither understand nor grasp the greatness of the coming test for the Ummah of Islam. They think trial lay only in the kind by which people were tried before, so they memorised its kinds and forms, and then they append the Dajjal to them as a follow-on. They know nothing of the trial of the 7, the 8 or the 9. Perhaps soon, by the power of Allah Almighty, they will know, understand and grasp, and on that day the pulpits will be sermon upon sermon and reminder upon reminder, with awe visible on the faces, tears shining in the eyes, and a clear, radiant love for Allah.""")

t(33, 2290, """Every wronged person will certainly be given victory, by Allah Almighty's leave .. When people are wronged they say: When? Indeed, injustice is a test for the wrongdoer and "when" is a test for the wronged! The supplication of the wronged, by Allah, by Allah, by Allah, is answered, if Allah wills, if Allah wants and if Allah permits .. It is among the supplications of the strongest tremor and sound, because it is proof of a challenge to Allah the Great that took place on earth .. For our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, to say to us: Do not wrong, and then we wrong, is a challenge to Allah Almighty in His earth .. So the supplication of the wronged on earth is a knocking on the King's door and a complaint to Him. Does the King see an injustice and then it is as if the injustice never happened? Far be it from Allah the Great, the King, our Lord. But as I said months ago about my experience with one of the aggressor YouTubers, who transgressed by slandering honor and left no evil word unsaid in front of everyone for 3 years: one day one of the brothers asked me about the answering of supplication against the wrongdoer, and I wrote that day that when the wrongdoer mocks Allah's threat, the wronged need not despair of Allah's help! Both are being tested. The wrongdoer is tested and the wronged is tested. As for the wrongdoer, he is tested: will he turn back, or will the demand of his self and its desire grow stronger in him? A wrongdoer may be given years of time to turn back and he does not. As for the wronged, he deposits the file of his case with""")

t(34, 150, """the King, and does not keep saying every hour: When .. when .. For he is being tested in his anger at the injustice done to him: will he respond .. will he transgress .. will he take his right by his hand or his tongue after depositing the file of his case with the King? Or will he be patient, awaiting the King's judgment? As we see, the test is not for the wrongdoer alone. Whoever is wronged and does not take his right by his hand or his tongue and deposits his case with his Lord must await the judgment without his soul becoming agitated and saying: The punishment is late .. the punishment is late .. That is not your business as a wronged person. Yes, the punishment is delayed, because the wrongdoer, for example, has a daughter he must support for a period of time before the punishment descends on him! Because the wrongdoer, for example, has a family, a family that did no wrong and needs him to establish for it a home or a farm to take refuge in at its time of need, so he must prepare for his family what it needs before the punishment befalls him! The world was not created for your sake, O wronged one, that you should say: I was wronged, I want my right now! No, the world was not created only for your needs. The world is complex .. It has very complex details .. It has entanglements hidden from no one and known to all .. The world is individual and collective destinies .. The wrongdoer wrongs, but this wrongdoer has a soul that has not yet completed its provision, and a family that has not yet completed what it is meant to have from this wrongdoer, and perhaps he will wrong others whom he has not yet wronged. So when your right comes to you early, you are asking for the worldly system to be disrupted for your sake! That is a strange thing! The world was not created only for the wronged, so that as soon as he is wronged his right is taken for him. It is natural for anger to remain in your chest. The wrongdoer's punishment may be postponed for a year, two or three while your chest is full of anger. Imagine a person who wakes in the morning to a creature slandering his honor in front of millions of people .. saying to him in front of millions of people: you trade in your wives .. Muslim women .. veiled .. who pray at night .. merely because he disagreed with that person .. And the wait for the punishment to descend on him goes on, but it is the wait of the forbearing, the confident, the deliberate, the one not preoccupied with "when"! The one who has no "when" in his daily life! But as a wronged person, whatever the kind of injustice done to you, do not blame yourself for being angry. That is natural.
The experiences of injustice people have been subjected to are many; injustice occurs daily, around the clock and without stop. I do not know the extent of injustice among people today; only our Lord the King knows. But it is frightening in extent, quantity and kind, terrifying and shattering, and whoever does not see it on earth is blind in sight and insight.""")

t(34, 1320, """People in this world are holders of rights before they are bearers of duties. A single smile on the face of a single small child means that there is a whole system working in secret to make this child safe, at peace and happy, living a normal life and receiving his rights as a child! And to make the grandfather safe! And to make the grandmother safe! And to keep the man and his wife in security! A system that sees what society does not see! That grasps what society does not grasp! That works behind the scenes! The unknown soldiers on whose shoulders states are built, societies become stable, justice prevails and all people without exception are happy! It is a system that does not rejoice as people rejoice, because it does not have the time people have! It is a system that finds no time to live people's lives! It finds no way to be safe from every kind of treachery, harm and targeting as people are safe .. It is the system that is always targeted .. because eliminating its members means shaking the system and perhaps crushing it .. A salute to every unknown soldier in this world who was and still is a lofty spirit, glad that it serves people and makes them happy, even if the body and self of its owner, man or woman, did not enjoy the same life and comfort as others! To these monotheist men and women, peace from us .. and peace be upon them on the day people stand before the Lord of the worlds!""")

t(36, 1195, """I have never found a (godly) scholar firmly grounded in the science of hadith, among the hadith scholars, to whom a contradiction between a hadith and a verse in the Book of Allah Almighty was raised, but that he said the hadith was weak in chain / text, or that the narrator was confused, or that the narrator forgot and did not hear well. As the Lady Aishah, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, once said: Abu Hurayrah misheard, when she was asked about the contradiction in the hadith "the child of adultery is the worst of the three" and the hadith's plain conflict with the Book of Allah Almighty. The hadith concerned one specific, particular child who harmed the Prophet ﷺ, so it was a ruling specific to a particular child; perhaps revelation informed the Prophet ﷺ that there was evil in this child's conduct .. This scrutiny and examination of hadiths is what protects the Ummah from falling into disasters. And the disasters are many; disastrous foundations were laid for them in people's lives, and upon them were built juristic understandings that were at times mistaken and at other times corrupt in argument. Thus the Ummah was lost for long centuries after the death of the first generation of the noble companions, to whom people referred for decisive words. After them came the mujtahids, who were right and wrong .. then wrong and right, and right and wrong .. In any case .. it is established for people more and more every day, through following the specialist scholars of the science of hadith in particular, that everything that contradicts the explicit Qur'an is not authentically from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So do not take the meaning of any hadith that conflicts with the explicit Qur'an from the mouth of non-specialists, for they, as hadith scholars, are more able, by the power of Allah Almighty, to prove to you the weakness of every hadith that conflicts with the explicit Book of Allah Almighty, the Great, our Lord.""")

t(36, 2030, """Honoring children comes through spouses treating each other well .. In the calm home the children are honored .. So fear Allah, O servants of Allah, men and women, regarding the offspring .. Except one who has been wronged, woman or man .. Perhaps Allah will make for him .. or make for her .. a way, a relief and a victory, and be kind and gentle to the children wherever they are""")

t(37, 890, """Girls are (a worry), yes, especially in this time of ours, because they are weak .. May Allah our Lord help fathers and mothers .. O young husbands .. O mothers-in-law .. Fear Allah .. Fear Allah regarding people's daughters .. And know that the punishment of injustice is immense on a day when regret will not avail. How many a husband has entered the Fire because of a wife! And how many a husband's mother has entered the Fire because of a son's wife! Fear Allah for your flesh on the Day of Resurrection .. for your skins .. Let no person come on the Day of Resurrection saying: I did not know, I had no idea this would happen to me .. On that day the screaming is loud .. pains and aches follow one another without stopping .. and the groaning and wailing in Hell go on without end .. And the poor wronged woman struts in bliss .. a crowned, pampered queen .. while the husband and his mother are wretched together in the Fire; son and mother keep each other company in the fire of Hell, insulting each other and cursing each other .. The son and his mother .. They even hit each other .. and spit on each other .. The son and his mother .. That is true and will be .. The girl they wronged looks at them and says: Praise be to Allah who took my right for me .. Rot in the Fire more and more .. This is the station you both deserve .. So let whoever has grown fond of injustice fear Allah, to save his skin, his flesh and his dignity!""")

t(37, 2545, """A bridge, then relief for us all, Allah Almighty willing .. And women have an ample share of life in the lands of their Ummah, by the power of Allah Almighty""")

t(38, 1385, """The hall for collecting Bayt al-Maqdis passports, by the power of our Lord""")

t(39, 225, """An artificial-intelligence image, not of a real child .. A weaned child crying .. In human relationships there is a weaning that people practice toward each other .. A very large number of people practice weaning toward each other .. Then when the axe falls on the head they are amazed that people move away from them .. The husband moving away from his wife .. the wife moving away from her husband .. brothers moving away from each other .. friends moving away from each other .. The cause is very clear, but it is hidden from them and they do not see it .. They discover the size of the mistake they made only when they reap the results, and the results are very disastrous .. The result is the weaning of one person from another .. Unfortunately, those who practice the behavior of weaning as a punishment for a wife .. or a punishment for a husband .. or a punishment for any person in their social surroundings do not know that weaning time after time after time ends in psychological weaning, which is a thousand times more dangerous than weaning of the other kinds .. Psychological weaning is very dangerous and its results are disastrous, because they strike the depth of a person's sense of dignity in a vital spot .. The one who practices the method of weaning on you time after time strikes you in your dignity, so you become angry for it and avenge it by his leaving your soul and turning into something ordinary .. He is present, fine .. He is absent, fine! Here people begin to reap the results of their wrong conduct, but it is a bitter harvest.""")

t(39, 1950, """Dear brothers .. In comment on one of today's comments .. There is no such thing as the art of Islamic architecture from a religious standpoint .. Using the term "Islamic architecture" as if it were a matter related to religion and legislation is a big mistake .. because this would mean that Muslims over 1447 years built their houses and everything in their cities according to Qur'anic texts telling them: build such-and-such wall this way, the ceiling must be like this and the door must be like this; and that of course is not true. The way of building has no relation to any verse in the Book of our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, nor to the sayings of the Prophet ﷺ. Rather, if the architecture of Muslims, as a model, method and architectural style, has been described as "Islamic architecture", that is only because those who founded this art were Muslims, no more and no less. It would have been more correct not to attach the word Islamic to the art of architecture, because that would cause confusion in the understanding of many people, as has indeed happened! Muslims have had an architectural art throughout history and to this day: in India and Pakistan it is other than Turkey's, in Turkey other than Egypt's and North Africa's, in the Arabian Peninsula other than all of them, in Yemen other than all those mentioned, and in Azerbaijan, Turkmenistan and the other Islamic countries of Central Asia there are different styles, forms and details! And before that, examples still stand, such as the Umayyad, Abbasid, Andalusian, Fatimid and Mamluk monuments! So where is the Islamic art of architecture? It is more correct to understand that the art of architecture is a purely human effort and a purely human ijtihad. So it is not fitting for you as a Muslim, when your Muslim neighbor builds a building in the Belgian style, to say that he has gone against Islam and against the Shari'ah! That is wrong talk .. Nor is it fitting, if you enter a Muslim city whose architecture is drawn from European art that has no crosses, no statues, no trait of unbelief and no hint of unbelief from near or""")

t(40, 150, """far, but is merely a Western architectural model, for you to say: I seek Allah's forgiveness, what is this?! That comes from not understanding realities correctly, and from minds being closed to grasping things correctly. The (Islamic) art of architecture, an imprecise expression but one people have grown used to, is a human ijtihad .. the ijtihad of humans .. humans who liked the idea of making a ceiling shaped like this .. and a wall shaped like this .. not to mention the environmental factors that have a wide and great effect on the building styles of all humans. When the European, the Turk and others, in all the lands of snow, made sloping roofs, did they make them sloping because the Torah and the Gospel contain texts on how the roof is to be built? The matter has nothing to do with religion; rather, rain made that inevitable for all the people of rainy lands and lands where heavy snow falls, even in the farthest east of Asia and in North America over thousands of years, where the tents of the native inhabitants were sloping, and even the houses of the Eskimos are sloping, where there was neither Torah nor Gospel! And Allah is the One whose help is sought.""")

t(40, 1800, """In a post this morning I spoke about the will of the people of the Fire and set out my view on it in detail. One of the dear brothers then raised a question about that will, as to its being a will in which the side of means is given to the people of the Fire, because of the verse the dear brother mentioned in his question; it is the very verse on whose meaning the reply here is built. I had said in my explanation of the will of the people of the Fire that it is a will without means, because means are entirely cut off from them in the Fire and forbidden to them, and it is merely a will of wishing and desire, no more. This is contrary to the view of the dear questioner, who held that the mere fact that they are returned after attempting to escape means that means are available to them to carry out their will, in success or failure. So I answered the dear brother at length to clear up the matter for him. Before copying my reply here for general benefit, it is important that we recall the word of our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, magnified in the heavens and the earth and exalted most high, about the situation the dear questioner asked about: the attempt of the people of the Fire to get out of it, and his considering that this means their will was followed by means they undertook, since attempting to escape is taking the means, from his point of view, which he put forward as discussion and not dispute, may Allah honor him. Whereas in truth, if we examine the matter, we will know that means are forbidden to them. We see in the Book of our Lord the word of our Great Lord, hallowed be His names: {"Whenever they want to get out of it, out of anguish, they are returned into it: taste the punishment of the burning"} .. We see that our Great Lord says "returned in it"! And not "returned to it". This noble verse had slipped my memory when I explained to the brother in my reply this morning to his question; then I remembered the verse and said: Glory be to our Great Lord. Our Great Lord says "returned in it" and not "returned to it", and this is a clear indication that means are not available at all for them to take. This is what I showed in the post where I spoke of the will of the people of the Fire. For if means were available to them to get out of it, some would succeed and some would fail, and it would not be possible for the wording of the verse to be "returned in it"; a rational and logical contradiction would arise on reading the verse. If means were available to the people of the Fire, so that some succeed in escaping and some fail, the verse would have to be "returned to it" .. with "returned to it" meaning those who succeeded in escaping and used means that enabled them to escape. But Allah Almighty, our Great Lord,""")

t(41, 150, """said "returned in it". This means that they try to escape while they are in it and never reach outside it, and this means the fall of all means there, and that means there are not created for them and not granted to them at all. Had means been created for them there, some would have succeeded in escaping outside it and been returned to it, and the noble verse would have been "returned to it" and not "returned in it".

And this was my reply to the dear questioner's question, for whoever wants more: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Perhaps there is a wall in it toward which they head, and outside the wall is not fire! Here they are not taking means, because the wall is in the same place. A movement counted as within the perimeter of the crisis is not counted as taking means. Taking means is to go outside the crisis to activate the tools, meaning you put at least one foot outside the crisis and so possess the means, even by 1%, outside the crisis. If taking means were to be decreed for them in the Fire, they would have to climb over the wall and get out of the Fire entirely and then be returned; then yes, they would have taken the means and left the crisis completely; or partially, by reaching the wall so that they are between the Fire and what is beyond it without leaving it entirely; then yes, their taking of means would occur. But what if the wall is curved, not vertical, and they try to climb it from below, hoping to rise to its top, and slide down the wall because it is curved, while they are inside the Fire? This is an attempt of a will to get out, as the verse mentions, an attempt that expresses a wish .. a wish to get out .. a will whose title is only a wish, with no taking of real or considerable means in it, because means are not permitted to exist at all in the Fire. So the word of our Great Lord: ("Whenever they want to get out of it") is not a wording of a will followed by real means, but a will of wishing. You want to become a pilot, you want; all you do, for example, is browse information on how to become a pilot, only that .. You do nothing else; here you have not activated the tools of means …""")

t(41, 1270, """As came in the report: And to the people return their affection and their blessing, the near of them and the far.""")

t(41, 2495, """Our brother, the man in the picture, says: (Islam's second universality does not begin except with conditions, among them that people commit adultery in the streets on the sidewalks completely naked, and this for him is the condition for the earth's being filled with injustice and oppression to come true); for our brother it is among the conditions for the earth's being filled with injustice and oppression to come true. The cause of this is what we all warned against throughout our gathering""")
